				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Tab pushed a lock of black, once red hair out of her eyes as she looked over the list of new recruits.  She was trying to keep up with the recent rise in applications caused by stress in the land.  The Gods had caused more hardship than usual and there were many who sought shelter in the forests with the wolves.
<br />

<br />
Her armor and hair once the colors of autum and a sign of her days as a solo scout were now the colors of sky, day and night, signaling her new position as part of the guild's raid forces.
<br />

<br />
A flash of light caught her eye before she bent back to her lists.  Glancing up again she saw a female warrior pass the last check point and turn two heavy bags over to the Quartermaster to be cleared and stowed in her new home.  Looking at the woman's weapons and armor - not to mention the stony look on her face - Tab knew who this applicant must be.
<br />

<br />
The slender druid rose in the fluid almost unnoticable motion of one long on scout duty as the warrior drew near.  Normally Tab extended a warm welcome to new comers and led them to Raveena's high tree ledge office, but not this time.  The veiled pain of the former leader of a guild struck too hard by famine and death was too sacred and fragile for her to breach.  She simply extended the necessary papers and nodded to the stair nearly hidden at the base of the huge tree.<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /></div></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
